+// LAB-SW lever 1 (lab only, not yet a patch): DOSAGS_SAVEMEM -- serialise the whole save into memory, then write it
+// with one fopen "wb" + fwrite + fclose. =0 keeps the streaming path below untouched; unset or anything else = 1.
+//
+// Exact by construction: the same serialiser writes the same bytes into a VectorStream instead of a BufferedStream.
+// Both seek with clamping to [0, end] and overwrite in place, so every seek-back patch (component headers, the
+// FileFormat block at offset 39, WriteBitmap's size and its Seek(end_pos, kSeekEnd) = clamp to end) lands at the
+// same offset; DeflateStream takes either base through Release/AttachStreamBase. The file is opened FIRST, exactly
+// as today (same truncation, same failure point before any serialisation); only what sits behind the Stream changes.
+// If the memory cannot be had (bad_alloc while reserving or growing), the already-open FileStream is wrapped in the
+// usual BufferedStream and the streaming path runs from the start: the partial memory image is discarded, and the
+// only state a second serialisation re-touches is DoBeforeSave's (idempotent copies). Counted as a fallback.
+long dos_savemem_mem = 0, dos_savemem_fallback = 0, dos_savemem_stream = 0, dos_savemem_short = 0;
+long dos_savemem_last_bytes = 0; int dos_savemem_last_path = 0;   // 0 stream (=0), 1 memory, 2 fallback
+int dos_savemem_mode_get()
